#
# FILE            memory_limit_small_budget_log.test
#
# AUTHOR          Ken Zangelin
#
# Copyright 2026 Seamware
#
# A budget below 1 MiB is said in KiB: --memoryLimit 1 makes the response size budget 1/16 of 1 MiB,
# 64 KiB, and the start-up line said "response size budget: 0 MiB" - a budget that is not none, read as
# none. Likewise the soft limit of the memory budget, 90 % of 1 MiB: "writes refused above 0 MiB". From
# 1 MiB on the text is MiB, as it was (corBase's corSizeText).
#
# Read from the start-up log (-v), the one place the budgets are said: a broker over its memory budget
# refuses the writes that would make a response large enough to show the 403's text.
#
# REQUIRE_FEATURE: RESPONSE_BUDGET
#
--NAME--
A 1 MiB memory budget (--memoryLimit 1): the start-up log says the budgets below 1 MiB in KiB, not "0 MiB"

--TAGS--
memory cli

--INIT--
corDbDrop
coraineStart --memoryLimit 1 -v

--RUN--

echo "01. The response size budget - 1/16 of 1 MiB"
echo "============================================"
grep -o "response size budget: .*" /tmp/coraine.CB.log
echo
echo


echo "02. The memory budget and its soft limit (90 %)"
echo "==============================================="
grep -o "memory budget: [0-9].*" /tmp/coraine.CB.log
echo
echo


--TEARDOWN--
coraineStop

--EXPECT--
01. The response size budget - 1/16 of 1 MiB
============================================
response size budget: 64 KiB (1/16 of the memory budget)


02. The memory budget and its soft limit (90 %)
===============================================
memory budget: 1 MiB (writes refused above 921 KiB)


